<title>HONG KONG: Liu Chong Hing 1996 net up 14.97 percent.</title>
<headline>Liu Chong Hing 1996 net up 14.97 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   125.0    vs 109.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    30.0     vs 30.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil	vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    476.38   vs 414.36</p>
<p>    Turnover		     2,533.26 vs 1,886.51 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 Liu Chong Hing Investment Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 14-21</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   April 29</p>
<p>NOTE - Liu Chong Hing engages in property development and investment, warehousing, banking and insurance services.</p>
<p>Turnover for 1995 is adjusted to include interest income, fees, commission and other revenue from banking operation. No adjustment has been made for the profit figure for 1995.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is 48 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 18 cents) vs same.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
